comfyui-am-vfx-tools — credits & attribution
============================================

The OIIO image read/write paths (`am_image_read.py`, `am_image_write.py`,
`_core/image_backend.py`) and the frame-pattern handling (`_core/sequence.py`)
started from sumitchatterjee13/nuke-nodes-comfyui:

    https://github.com/sumitchatterjee13/nuke-nodes-comfyui

Specifically: that repo's `io_nodes.py` (`read_image_oiio` /
`write_image_oiio`) and its `parse_frame_pattern` / `expand_frame_pattern`
/ `detect_sequence` helpers gave us the OIIO + frame-token foundations.

The upstream pack is MIT-licensed; the original copyright notice applies
to the derived portions.

This is a code-import (not a fork). The implementation has been rewritten
from scratch and extended substantially:

  * Full OCIO 2.x ColorProcessor pipeline (built-in Studio / CG fallbacks,
    layered config loader, family-grouped colorspace dropdowns) wired
    through every read/write path.
  * PyAV-backed video read/write (`am_video_read.py`, `am_video_write.py`,
    `_core/video_backend.py`) — full codec coverage (h264 / h265 / prores /
    dnxhr / vp9), alpha-bearing pixel formats on read+write where the
    codec supports it (prores 4444), frame-accurate seek.
  * `os.scandir`-based sequence scan (`detect_sequence_range`) replacing
    the upstream `glob.glob` approach — significant performance win on
    NFS / large directories.
  * Embedded ComfyUI workflow metadata in EXR / PNG (`comfyui/prompt`,
    `comfyui/workflow` keys) for round-trip recovery.
  * Frame-mode / range / missing-frame-policy / edge-extrapolation
    knobs not present upstream.
  * OpenCV-backed reformat (`_core/reformat.py`) with five filters,
    4-channel alpha-preserving.
  * Nuke-style Grade math (`_core/grade.py`).
  * Process-global seed registry (`_core/seed_registry.py`) addressing
    a render-farm reproducibility issue documented at
    comfyanonymous/ComfyUI#11905.
  * Native OS file dialog + workfile-io workflow-management subsystem
    (`_filechooser/`, `routes_workfile.py`, `web/workfile-io.js`) —
    independent of the upstream and added here.
